# ═══ Layer 0: 错误面 ═══
id:                     DRAFT-f2fs-tools-kernel-backed-filesystem-validation
trigger_tool:           configure|make|ioctl|mount|test|runtime
phase:                  configuration|testing|runtime
error_signature:        F2FS_IOC_.*(ENOTTY|EOPNOTSUPP)|mount.*f2fs.*(EPERM|EACCES|ENODEV)

# ═══ Layer 1: 识别层 ═══
severity:               2
category:               kernel, ohos, portability, testing
match_keywords:         F2FS_IOC, f2fs_io, loop mount, fsstress, filesystem image, HarmonyOS
title:                  Separate image-level checks from kernel-facing filesystem validation

# ═══ Layer 2: 诊断层 ═══
root_cause:             F2FS image tools can operate on regular files, while ioctl, mount, resize-under-mount, and power-loss paths depend on kernel support, privilege, and a disposable device; build or --version success proves only the user-space binary contract
affected_scope:         Linux filesystem utility packages that ship image tools plus direct filesystem ioctl or privileged mount/stress tests
verification_cmd:      mkfs.f2fs -f <scratch-image> && fsck.f2fs -f <scratch-image>; separately run the upstream mount/ioctl matrix on a compatible kernel and isolated device

# ═══ Layer 3: 方案层 ═══
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           split-image-and-kernel-validation
rec_description:        Keep regular-file formatter/checker consumers separate from privileged kernel-facing scenarios and report both result sets explicitly
rec_command:            mkfs.f2fs -f "$TMPDIR/f2fs.img" && fsck.f2fs -f "$TMPDIR/f2fs.img"; run the pinned upstream matrix on an isolated F2FS-capable device
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:     false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern:       --version.*(mount|ioctl)|version.*kernel.*PASS
forbid_1_reason:        A version or help command does not exercise the mounted filesystem's ioctl contract or kernel implementation
forbid_1_consequence:   A user-space build is incorrectly presented as proof that the target kernel supports F2FS operations
forbid_2_pattern:       mount.*(without.*isolated|shared.*mount)|spo_test.*\/dev\/sdb1
forbid_2_reason:        The upstream power-loss scenario writes to a raw block device and forces a reboot
forbid_2_consequence:   A shared or non-disposable target can lose data or reboot an unrelated service

principles:             R34, R51
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E265
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

